; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Binary Tree
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, tree, fractal, color
; SUMMARY:  Grows a tree in which every branch splits into two smaller branches.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Draws a brown trunk that splits in two. Each half splits in two
;   again, and again, until the twigs are tiny and turn green like
;   leaves. The whole tree comes from one short procedure.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the numbers on the last line to grow a taller
;   tree or to open the branches wider.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * recursion: a procedure that calls itself
;   * a stopping rule so the recursion ends
;   * returning the turtle to where it started (state saving)
;   * choosing a pen color and pen size from an input
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the angle 25 to 15 or 40 and watch the shape change.
;   * Change 0.7 to 0.6 or 0.78 in BRANCH. What happens to the tree?
;   * Make the leaves pink for a cherry tree in spring.
; ============================================================

; BRANCH draws one branch and the two smaller trees that sit on it.
; :len is how long this branch is, :angle how far the two children lean.
to branch :len :angle
  ; The stopping rule. Without it the turtle would draw smaller and
  ; smaller branches forever.
  if :len < 5 [stop]
  ; Thick, brown wood near the ground; thin, green twigs at the tips.
  setpensize :len / 10
  ifelse :len < 15 [setpencolor [60 170 60]] [setpencolor [120 75 40]]
  forward :len
  ; The left child
  left :angle
  branch :len * 0.7 :angle
  ; The right child: turn twice as far to swing past the middle
  right 2 * :angle
  branch :len * 0.7 :angle
  ; Undo the turns and walk back down. Because every BRANCH puts the
  ; turtle back exactly where it found it, the parent can carry on.
  left :angle
  back :len
end

; TREE moves the turtle to the bottom of the screen and starts growing.
to tree :size :angle
  penup setxy 0 -270 setheading 0 pendown
  branch :size :angle
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [235 245 255]
tree 130 25
